topkapi_setup/params.py: the seven soil/land-cover rasters generate_param_file
reads (soil_depth, Ks, theta_r, theta_s, n_o, psi_b, lambda), each snapped to
the terrain mask, range-validated, with params_manifest.json for M4.

- Rawls/Brakensiek Brooks-Corey defaults by USDA texture class; psi_b written
  in mm to match the solver's Green-Ampt path (ref cell_param ~332).
- SANLC 2020 n_o defaults by class group; editable code->group crosswalk.
- Pluggable source: soil-form/land-cover rasters, or --uniform-* first pass.
- Soil depth: --soil-depth takes a continuous depth raster (m);
  subcommand reclasses an HWSD v2.0 SMU-code raster + SMU->depth CSV into that
  raster (cm->m). SoilGrids works via the same --soil-depth input.
- CLI now has  and  subcommands.

topkapi_setup/viz.py: params panel (plot_params), single-raster (plot_raster)
and per-raster (plot_each / --each) views; CLI auto-detects terrain vs params.

topkapi_setup/USAGE.md: task-oriented CLI-first usage doc backfilling M0-M2
(incl. the HWSD workflow and the viewer), with the module contract new stages
must follow. Full suite: 30 passed.
